-- title:
--   Scheduling control policies, admissibility, work conservation, costs, and the proposed preemptive policy (P-SCP)
-- statement:
--   This file defines the policies of the $n$-th system and their costs.
--
--   **Policies** (Definition 1). A **P-SCP** of the $n$-th system started from $X^{0,n}\in\mathbb Z^k_+$ is a càdlàg process $\Psi^n$ (the numbers in service) with a controlled process $X^n$ (the numbers in system). They satisfy the constraints (6) — $\Psi^n(t)\in\mathbb Z^k_+$, $\Phi^n(t)=X^n(t)-\Psi^n(t)\in\mathbb Z^k_+$ and $\sum_i\Psi^n_i(t)\le n$ — and the system equations
--   $$
--   X^n_i(t)=X^{0,n}_i+A^n_i(t)-R^n_i\Big(\int_0^t(X^n_i-\Psi^n_i)(s)\,ds\Big)-S^n_i\Big(\int_0^t\Psi^n_i(s)\,ds\Big).\qquad(7)
--   $$
--
--   **Admissibility** (Definition 2). Let $T^n_i(t)=\int_0^t\Psi^n_i$ and $\mathring T^n_i(t)=\int_0^t\Phi^n_i$. Let $\mathcal F^n_t$ be generated by $A^n_i(s),S^n_i(T^n_i(s)),R^n_i(\mathring T^n_i(s)),\Phi^n_i(s),\Psi^n_i(s),X^n_i(s)$ for $s\le t$, and $\mathcal G^n_t$ by the increments $A^n_i(\tau^n_i(t)+u)-A^n_i(\tau^n_i(t))$, $S^n_i(T^n_i(t)+u)-S^n_i(T^n_i(t))$ and $R^n_i(\mathring T^n_i(t)+u)-R^n_i(\mathring T^n_i(t))$ for $u\ge0$. The policy is **admissible** if
--   1. $\mathcal F^n_t$ is independent of $\mathcal G^n_t$ for every $t$, and
--   2. the restarted processes $S^n_i(T^n_i(t)+\cdot)-S^n_i(T^n_i(t))$ and $R^n_i(\mathring T^n_i(t)+\cdot)-R^n_i(\mathring T^n_i(t))$ are equal in law to $S^n_i$ and $R^n_i$.
--
--   **Work conservation** (Definition 3) is $(\mathbb 1\cdot X^n(t)-n)^+=\mathbb 1\cdot\Phi^n(t)$ for $t\ge0$.
--
--   **Scalings.** With $\rho_i=\lambda_i/\mu_i$:
--   - $\hat\Phi^n=n^{-1/2}\Phi^n$, $\hat\Psi^n_i=n^{-1/2}(\Psi^n_i-\rho_in)$, $\hat X^n_i=n^{-1/2}(X^n_i-\rho_in)$;
--   - $\bar\Psi^n=n^{-1}\Psi^n$, $\bar\Phi^n=n^{-1}\Phi^n$;
--   - $\hat X^{0,n}=n^{-1/2}(X^{0,n}-\rho n)$.
--
--   **Costs.** The cost (20) of a policy is
--   $$
--   C^n=E\int_0^\infty e^{-\gamma t}\tilde L(\hat\Phi^n(t),\hat\Psi^n(t))\,dt.
--   $$
--   Its form in the variables of Section 4 is $E\int_0^\infty e^{-\gamma t}L(\hat X^n_t,u^n_t)\,dt$, where $u^n=\Phi^n/(\mathbb 1\cdot X^n-n)^+$ when $\mathbb 1\cdot X^n>n$ and $u^n=u_0\in\mathbb S^k$ otherwise (47).
--
--   **The proposed P-SCP** (pp. 18–19). Given $h:\mathbb R^k\to\mathbb S^k$, a state $X\in\mathbb Z^k_+$, $q=(\mathbb 1\cdot X-n)^+$ and $\hat X=n^{-1/2}(X-\rho n)$, the policy sets the queue vector as follows.
--   - If $X_i\ge q$ for all $i$ (condition (31)), then $\Phi=\Theta[q\,h(\hat X)]$. Here the rounding map $\Theta$ of (29)–(30) keeps $\lfloor y_i\rfloor$ for the first $k-1$ classes and puts the rounding remainder on class $k$.
--   - Otherwise $\Phi$ follows the work-conserving static priority rule in which class $k$ is served first, then class $k-1$, and so on.
--
--   The policy then serves $\Psi=X-\Phi$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** A policy is a pair of real-valued processes $(\Psi,X)$ on $\Omega\times\mathbb R$. Integrality, the constraints and (7) are required for every $\omega$ and $t\ge0$. Lebesgue integrability of $\Psi_i$ and $\Phi_i$ on $[0,t]$ is stated explicitly; the paper notes on p. 11 that it holds automatically. Each $\Psi_i(t)$ is required to be a random variable. Laws of restarted processes are those of their paths on $[0,\infty)$. Costs are lower Lebesgue integrals in $[0,\infty]$; the integrand is nonnegative for work-conserving policies by (21), (47) and Assumption 2(i). The paper's class $i$ is Lean index $i-1$, so "class $k$" is the last index. The priority rule is written in closed form as $\Psi_i=\min(X_i,(n-\sum_{j>i}X_j)^+)$.
-- source:
--   Atar, Mandelbaum & Reiman, Scheduling a Multi Class Queue with Many Exponential Servers: Asymptotic Optimality in Heavy Traffic, arXiv:math/0407058v1 (reprint of Ann. Appl. Probab. 14(3), 2004), p. 10 (4)-(7), pp. 11-12 Definitions 1-2 and (8)-(10), pp. 13-15 rescaled processes, Definition 3 (18), (20)-(21), pp. 18-19 the P-SCP (28)-(31), p. 30 (47)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BellWilliams2001_ThresholdPolicy_Paths
import Definitions.Def_ManyServerQED_Scheduling_Diffusion
import Definitions.Def_ManyServerQED_Scheduling_Model

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped ENNReal NNReal

namespace ManyServerQED.Scheduling

open BellWilliams2001.ThresholdPolicy

/-!
Atar, Mandelbaum & Reiman (2004), §2.1–§2.6 (pp. 9–19) and (47) (p. 30): scheduling control
policies of the `n`-th system, admissibility, work conservation, the rescaled processes, the
costs, and the proposed preemptive policy (P-SCP).

A policy of the `n`-th system is a pair `(Ψ, X)` of processes `Ω → ℝ → (Fin k → ℝ)`
(`Ψ ω t i = Ψⁿᵢ(t)(ω)`, the number of class-`i` customers in service; `X ω t i = Xⁿᵢ(t)(ω)`, the
number of class-`i` customers in the system); the queue lengths are `Φ = X − Ψ` (5). Only times
`t ≥ 0` matter.
-/

/-- `Tⁿᵢ(t) = ∫₀ᵗ Ψⁿᵢ(s) ds` (8), p. 11: the total service effort given to class `i` up to `t`. -/
noncomputable def busyTime {Ω : Type*} {k : ℕ} (Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) (ω : Ω) (i : Fin k)
    (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ s in (0 : ℝ)..t, Ψ ω s i

/-- `T̊ⁿᵢ(t) = ∫₀ᵗ Φⁿᵢ(s) ds = ∫₀ᵗ (Xⁿᵢ(s) − Ψⁿᵢ(s)) ds` (8), p. 11: the total time spent in queue
`i` up to `t`, summed over customers. -/
noncomputable def queueTime {Ω : Type*} {k : ℕ} (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) (ω : Ω) (i : Fin k)
    (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ s in (0 : ℝ)..t, (X ω s i - Ψ ω s i)

/-- An SCP is **work-conserving** (Definition 3, (18), p. 15):
`(𝟙 · Xⁿ(t) − n)⁺ = 𝟙 · Φⁿ(t)` for all `t ≥ 0`. -/
def IsWorkConserving {Ω : Type*} {k : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ ω t, 0 ≤ t → max (∑ i, X ω t i - n) 0 = ∑ i, (X ω t i - Ψ ω t i)

/-- `Φ̂ⁿᵢ(t) = n^{−1/2}Φⁿᵢ(t)` (p. 13). -/
noncomputable def Phihat {Ω : Type*} {k : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ)
    (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) (i : Fin k) : ℝ :=
  (X ω t i - Ψ ω t i) / Real.sqrt n

/-- `Ψ̄ⁿᵢ(t) = n^{−1}Ψⁿᵢ(t)` (p. 13). -/
noncomputable def Psibar {Ω : Type*} {k : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ)
    (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) (i : Fin k) : ℝ :=
  Ψ ω t i / n

/-- `Φ̄ⁿᵢ(t) = n^{−1}Φⁿᵢ(t)` (p. 13). -/
noncomputable def Phibar {Ω : Type*} {k : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ)
    (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) (i : Fin k) : ℝ :=
  (X ω t i - Ψ ω t i) / n

/-- The `𝕊^k`-valued process `uⁿ` of (47) (p. 30): `uⁿ = Φⁿ/(𝟙 · Xⁿ − n)⁺` if `𝟙 · Xⁿ − n > 0` and
`uⁿ = u₀` otherwise, for a fixed `u₀ ∈ 𝕊^k`. -/
noncomputable def uProc {Ω : Type*} {k : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (u0 : Fin k → ℝ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ)
    (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) :
    Fin k → ℝ :=
  if 0 < ∑ i, X ω t i - n then fun i => (X ω t i - Ψ ω t i) / (∑ j, X ω t j - n) else u0

/-- The rounding map `Θ` of (29)–(30) (p. 18): for `y ∈ ℝ^k_+` write `yᵢ = ⌊yᵢ⌋ + δᵢ` and set
`zᵢ = ⌊yᵢ⌋` for the classes `i = 1, …, k − 1` and `z_k = y_k + ∑_{i=1}^{k−1} δᵢ` for the last
class (Lean index `k − 1`). It preserves `𝟙 · y` and maps `{y ∈ ℝ^k_+ : 𝟙 · y ∈ ℤ}` into `ℤ^k_+`. -/
noncomputable def roundMap {k : ℕ} (y : Fin k → ℝ) : Fin k → ℝ :=
  fun i => if (i : ℕ) + 1 = k then
      y i + ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun j : Fin k => (j : ℕ) + 1 ≠ k), (y j - ⌊y j⌋)
    else (⌊y i⌋ : ℝ)

/-- The static priority rule used by the P-SCP when (31) fails (p. 19): class `i` has priority `i`,
the higher `i` the higher the priority, and the rule is work-conserving. Servers go first to the
last class, then to the next, and so on:
`Ψᵢ = min(Xᵢ, (n − ∑_{j > i} Xⱼ)⁺)`, and the queue is `Φ = X − Ψ`. -/
noncomputable def priorityPhi {k : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (X : Fin k → ℕ) : Fin k → ℝ :=
  fun i => (X i : ℝ) -
    min (X i : ℝ) (max ((n : ℝ) - ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun j : Fin k => i < j), (X j : ℝ)) 0)

namespace SystemSequence

variable {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {k : ℕ} (M : SystemSequence Ω k)

/-- `Ψ` and `X` solve the system equations (7) of the `n`-th system started from the integer
initial state `X^{0,n} = X0` under the constraints (6) (p. 10):
* `Ψⁿ(t)` and `Xⁿ(t) − Ψⁿ(t) = Φⁿ(t)` take values in `ℤ^k_+` and `∑ᵢ Ψⁿᵢ(t) ≤ n` ((1), (6);
  the processes count customers, p. 9, and `Bⁿ` has increments in `ℤ`, p. 10);
* the integrals in (7) are finite (Lebesgue integrability on `[0, t]`, which p. 11 notes follows
  from `Ψⁿᵢ ≤ n` and `Φⁿᵢ(t) ≤ X^{0,n} + Aⁿᵢ(t)`);
* (7) `Xⁿᵢ(t) = X^{0,n}ᵢ + Aⁿᵢ(t) − Rⁿᵢ(∫₀ᵗ (Xⁿᵢ − Ψⁿᵢ)) − Sⁿᵢ(∫₀ᵗ Ψⁿᵢ)`, for every `ω` and `t ≥ 0`. -/
structure IsControlled (n : ℕ) (X0 : Fin k → ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) : Prop where
  psi_int : ∀ ω t i, 0 ≤ t → ∃ m : ℤ, Ψ ω t i = m
  phi_int : ∀ ω t i, 0 ≤ t → ∃ m : ℤ, X ω t i - Ψ ω t i = m
  psi_nonneg : ∀ ω t i, 0 ≤ t → 0 ≤ Ψ ω t i
  phi_nonneg : ∀ ω t i, 0 ≤ t → 0 ≤ X ω t i - Ψ ω t i
  servers : ∀ ω t, 0 ≤ t → ∑ i, Ψ ω t i ≤ n
  integrable : ∀ ω i t, 0 ≤ t →
    IntervalIntegrable (fun s => Ψ ω s i) volume 0 t ∧
      IntervalIntegrable (fun s => X ω s i - Ψ ω s i) volume 0 t
  eq7 : ∀ ω t i, 0 ≤ t →
    X ω t i = X0 i + M.A n i ω t - M.R n i ω (queueTime X Ψ ω i t) - M.S n i ω (busyTime Ψ ω i t)

/-- `Ψ` is a **preemptive resume scheduling control policy (P-SCP)** of the `n`-th system with
controlled process `X` (Definition 1(i), p. 11): a stochastic process (each `Ψⁿᵢ(t)` is a random
variable) with càdlàg paths, such that `X` satisfies (7) and the constraints (6) hold. -/
structure IsSCP (n : ℕ) (X0 : Fin k → ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) : Prop where
  controlled : M.IsControlled n X0 X Ψ
  cadlag : ∀ ω i, IsCadlag (fun t => Ψ ω t i)
  meas : ∀ t i, Measurable (fun ω => Ψ ω t i)

/-- The information `Fⁿ_t` available at time `t` (9), p. 11:
`σ{Aⁿᵢ(s), Sⁿᵢ(Tⁿᵢ(s)), Rⁿᵢ(T̊ⁿᵢ(s)), Φⁿᵢ(s), Ψⁿᵢ(s), Xⁿᵢ(s) : i ∈ K, s ≤ t}` (times `s ∈ [0, t]`). -/
noncomputable abbrev pastInfo (n : ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) (t : ℝ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ (i : Fin k) (s : ℝ) (_ : s ∈ Set.Icc 0 t),
    (MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => M.A n i ω s) inferInstance ⊔
      MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => M.S n i ω (busyTime Ψ ω i s)) inferInstance ⊔
      MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => M.R n i ω (queueTime X Ψ ω i s)) inferInstance ⊔
      MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => X ω s i - Ψ ω s i) inferInstance ⊔
      MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => Ψ ω s i) inferInstance ⊔
      MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => X ω s i) inferInstance)

/-- The future information `Gⁿ_t` (10), p. 11:
`σ{Aⁿᵢ(τⁿᵢ(t) + u) − Aⁿᵢ(τⁿᵢ(t)), Sⁿᵢ(Tⁿᵢ(t) + u) − Sⁿᵢ(Tⁿᵢ(t)), Rⁿᵢ(T̊ⁿᵢ(t) + u) − Rⁿᵢ(T̊ⁿᵢ(t)) : i ∈ K, u ≥ 0}`,
with `τⁿᵢ(t)` the first class-`i` arrival time no earlier than `t`. -/
noncomputable abbrev futureInfo (n : ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) (t : ℝ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ (i : Fin k) (u : ℝ) (_ : 0 ≤ u),
    (MeasurableSpace.comap
        (fun ω => M.A n i ω (M.nextArrival n i ω t + u) - M.A n i ω (M.nextArrival n i ω t))
        inferInstance ⊔
      MeasurableSpace.comap
        (fun ω => M.S n i ω (busyTime Ψ ω i t + u) - M.S n i ω (busyTime Ψ ω i t)) inferInstance ⊔
      MeasurableSpace.comap
        (fun ω => M.R n i ω (queueTime X Ψ ω i t + u) - M.R n i ω (queueTime X Ψ ω i t))
        inferInstance)

/-- A scheduling control policy is **admissible** (Definition 2, p. 12) if
(i) for each `t ≥ 0`, `Fⁿ_t` is independent of `Gⁿ_t`;
(ii) for each `i` and `t ≥ 0`, the process `Sⁿᵢ(Tⁿᵢ(t) + ·) − Sⁿᵢ(Tⁿᵢ(t))` is equal in law to
`Sⁿᵢ(·)`, and `Rⁿᵢ(T̊ⁿᵢ(t) + ·) − Rⁿᵢ(T̊ⁿᵢ(t))` is equal in law to `Rⁿᵢ(·)` (laws of the paths on
`[0, ∞)`, product σ-algebra). -/
structure IsAdmissible (n : ℕ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) : Prop where
  indep : ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → Indep (M.pastInfo n X Ψ t) (M.futureInfo n X Ψ t) M.P
  service_law : ∀ (i : Fin k) (t : ℝ), 0 ≤ t →
    IdentDistrib
      (fun ω (u : ℝ≥0) => M.S n i ω (busyTime Ψ ω i t + u) - M.S n i ω (busyTime Ψ ω i t))
      (fun ω (u : ℝ≥0) => M.S n i ω u) M.P M.P
  abandon_law : ∀ (i : Fin k) (t : ℝ), 0 ≤ t →
    IdentDistrib
      (fun ω (u : ℝ≥0) => M.R n i ω (queueTime X Ψ ω i t + u) - M.R n i ω (queueTime X Ψ ω i t))
      (fun ω (u : ℝ≥0) => M.R n i ω u) M.P M.P

/-- `Ψ̂ⁿᵢ(t) = n^{−1/2}(Ψⁿᵢ(t) − ρᵢn)` (p. 13). -/
noncomputable def Psihat (n : ℕ) (Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) (i : Fin k) : ℝ :=
  (Ψ ω t i - M.rho i * n) / Real.sqrt n

/-- `X̂ⁿᵢ(t) = n^{−1/2}(Xⁿᵢ(t) − ρᵢn)` (p. 13). -/
noncomputable def Xhat (n : ℕ) (X : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) (i : Fin k) : ℝ :=
  (X ω t i - M.rho i * n) / Real.sqrt n

/-- The rescaled initial state `X̂^{0,n} = n^{−1/2}(X^{0,n} − ρn)` (pp. 13, 20). -/
noncomputable def Xhat0 (n : ℕ) (X0 : Fin k → ℕ) : Fin k → ℝ :=
  fun i => ((X0 i : ℝ) - M.rho i * n) / Real.sqrt n

/-- The cost (20) (p. 15) of an SCP of the `n`-th system:
`Cⁿ = E ∫₀^∞ e^{−γt} L̃(Φ̂ⁿ(t), Ψ̂ⁿ(t)) dt`, an iterated lower Lebesgue integral in `[0, ∞]`. For a
work-conserving SCP the integrand equals `L(X̂ⁿ(t), uⁿ(t)) ≥ 0` by (21), (47) and Assumption 2(i),
so `ENNReal.ofReal` loses nothing. -/
noncomputable def queueCost (Lt : (Fin k → ℝ) → (Fin k → ℝ) → ℝ) (γ : ℝ) (n : ℕ)
    (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∫⁻ ω, ∫⁻ t in Set.Ioi (0 : ℝ),
    ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-γ * t) * Lt (Phihat n X Ψ ω t) (M.Psihat n Ψ ω t)) ∂volume ∂M.P

/-- The cost in the variables `(X̂ⁿ, uⁿ)` (Theorem 4, p. 31):
`E ∫₀^∞ e^{−γt} L(X̂ⁿ_t, uⁿ_t) dt`, an iterated lower Lebesgue integral in `[0, ∞]`. -/
noncomputable def queueCostL (L : (Fin k → ℝ) → (Fin k → ℝ) → ℝ) (γ : ℝ) (n : ℕ)
    (u0 : Fin k → ℝ) (X Ψ : Ω → ℝ → Fin k → ℝ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∫⁻ ω, ∫⁻ t in Set.Ioi (0 : ℝ),
    ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-γ * t) * L (M.Xhat n X ω t) (uProc n u0 X Ψ ω t)) ∂volume ∂M.P

/-- The queue vector `Φ = F̃ₙ(X)` set by the **proposed P-SCP** (pp. 18–19) at state `X ∈ ℤ^k_+`,
given a map `h : ℝ^k → 𝕊^k`: with `q = (𝟙 · X − n)⁺` and `X̂ = n^{1/2}(n⁻¹X − ρ)`,
* if (31) holds, i.e. `Xᵢ ≥ q` for every `i`, then `Φ = Θ[q h(X̂)]` (29);
* otherwise `Φ` is set by the priority policy `priorityPhi`.
The policy serves `Ψ = X − Φ` (p. 19). -/
noncomputable def pscpPhi (h : (Fin k → ℝ) → (Fin k → ℝ)) (n : ℕ) (X : Fin k → ℕ) : Fin k → ℝ :=
  let q : ℝ := max (∑ i, (X i : ℝ) - n) 0
  let xh : Fin k → ℝ := fun i => ((X i : ℝ) - M.rho i * n) / Real.sqrt n
  if ∀ i, q ≤ (X i : ℝ) then roundMap (fun i => q * h xh i) else priorityPhi n X

end SystemSequence

end ManyServerQED.Scheduling


